
# Python virtual environment
.venv/
venv/
env/

# Python cache
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class

# Jupyter
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# Environment variables and secrets
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# ChromaDB databases
chroma_db/
backend/chroma_db/

# SQLite databases
*.db
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3

# Uploaded documents
backend/uploads/*
!backend/uploads/.gitkeep

# Document registry (local data)
backend/document_registry.json

# Frontend dependencies
frontend/node_modules/

# Build output
frontend/dist/
frontend/build/

# Logs
*.log
logs/

# Editor settings
.vscode/
.idea/

# OS files
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Temporary files
*.tmp
*.bak
```

## 3. Keep these important files

Your GitHub repository should contain approximately this structure:

<CodeBlock language="text">
Local-AI-Knowledge-Assistant/
│
├── backend/
│   ├── embeddings/
│   │   └── embedding_model.py
│   ├── ingestion/
│   │   ├── pdf_loader.py
│   │   ├── text_splitter.py
│   │   └── ...
│   ├── rag/
│   │   ├── generator.py
│   │   ├── retriever.py
│   │   └── test_rag.py
│   ├── services/
│   ├── vectorstore/
│   │   └── chroma_db.py
│   ├── database.py
│   ├── main.py
│   └── requirements.txt
│
├── frontend/
│   ├── public/
│   ├── src/
│   │   ├── App.jsx
│   │   ├── App.css
│   │   ├── index.css
│   │   └── main.jsx
│   ├── package.json
│   ├── package-lock.json
│   └── index.html
│
├── .gitignore
└── README.md
